    "body": "### Additional observation\n\n- Run: https://github.com/growilabs/growi/actions/runs/33640347248\n- Job: ci-app-test-integration (24.x, 8.0, 8, 8.19.16)\n- Commit: 950bfe99128e129a78dc394c7f79784c1ddb015e\n- Date: 2026-09-02T14:10:38Z\n\n```\nFAIL   app-integration  src/server/routes/apiv3/g2g-transfer-key-keep-alive.integ.ts > receive route \u2014 transfer key keep-alive > while the source builds the archive > the source keeps the destination's key alive, and stops once the archive is ready\nAssertionError: expected 1788358779033 to be greater than 1788358779033\n \u276f src/server/routes/apiv3/g2g-transfer-key-keep-alive.integ.ts:332:29\n    330|       // archive itself, so a long export runs the key out before the \u2026\n    331|       // over at all \u2014 and then not one byte of the transfer has arriv\u2026\n    332|       expect(earlyInExport).toBeGreaterThan(before);\n       |                             ^\n    333|       expect(laterInExport).toBeGreaterThan(earlyInExport);\n```\n\nSame-commit divergence: the push/merge-queue run of this identical commit (https://github.com/growilabs/growi/actions/runs/33640338874) ran the same job and it **passed**. PR #11837 is unrelated to this test file (diff/PR mismatch, \u2460). The assertion failure is a clock-tie (`expected N to be greater than N`), consistent with timing-based non-determinism.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
